   "unmapped": [
    "V_T is the l2 path-length variation B_T = sum_t ||theta_t - theta_{t+1}||_2 of the linear parameter"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In each round $t \\in [T]$, an action set $\\cX_t \\in \\mathbb{R}^d$ is given to the learner and it has to choose an action $X_t \\in \\cX_t$. Then, the reward $Y_t = \\langle X_t, \\theta_t^{\\star} \\rangle + \\eta_t$ is observed ... $\\eta_t$ is a conditionally 1-subGaussian random variable. The non-stationary assumption allows unknown parameter $\\theta_t^{\\star}$ to be time-variant within total variation budget $B_T = \\sum_{t=1}^{T-1} \\|\\theta_{t}^{\\star} - \\theta_{t+1}^{\\star}\\|_2$. ... assume $\\|\\theta_t^{\\star}\\|_2 \\le 1$, for all $x\\in \\cX_t$, $\\|x\\|_2 \\le 1$"
  },
